    <GaugingStation location="Frampton Cotterell" name="Frome (Bristol)" number="53026">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Crump profile weir opened in 1978 with pumping station upstream of gauging station.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Full range structure, but drowns out at high flows. Estimated 100-year flow contained by structure and it appears to have been over-designed. One theoretical rating applied across period of record. Gaugings can be difficult at site due to deep and slow moving water upstream. The site also suffers from siltation behind the weir.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Station opened in 1978. Crump profile weir, crest 7.5m broad.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2023 (WINFAP Files v12).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Detention lakes upstream of gauge. Pumping station upstream of gauging station.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Geology is mainly Coal Measures to the east of the River Frome, and Lias to the west. Responsive catchment, however detention lakes 4 to 6km upstream may truncate peaks. Land use is predominantly rural contains the town of Yate. No major changes to catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged close to AMAX3. All flows contained with a reasonable fit to gaugings. No bypassing reported." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
